{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H0.5x;1. WORK SHALL CONFORM TO ALL APPLICABLE CODES AND ORDINANCES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: BUILDING, PLUMBING, ELECTRICAL, AND MECHANICAL CODES. \P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;2. ANY ERRORS, OMISS
  3
IONS, OR CONFLICTS FOUND WITHIN THESE DRAWINGS SHALL BE BROUGHT TO THE ATTENTION OF THE OWNER OR THEIR REPRESENTATIVE BEFORE PROCEEDING WITH THE WORK.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;3. DO NOT SCALE THESE DRAWINGS. WRITTEN DIMEN
  3
SIONS TAKE PRECEDENCE OVER MEASUREMENTS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;4. DIMENSIONS ARE TAKEN FROM FACE OF FRAMING LUMBER, FACE OF CONCRETE/ MASONRY, CENTER OF COLUMN, AND CENTERLINE OF FIXTURE, UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\P\fLuc
  3
ida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;5. ALL DIMENSIONS NOTED "VERIFY IN FIELD (V.I.F.)" SHALL BE MEASURED BY THE CONTRACTOR PRIOR TO CONSTRUCTION. REPORT ANY DISCREPANCIES TO THE OWNER OR THEIR REPRESENTATIVE.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34
  3
; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;6. DETAILS SHOWN ARE TYPICAL. SIMILAR DETAILS APPLY IN SIMILAR SITUATIONS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;7. IN THE CASE OF DISCREPANCIES WITHIN DESCRIPTIONS OF SIMILAR ITEMS, PRECEDENCE SHALL BE GIVEN 
  3
TO NOTES & DRAWINGS OF GREATER DETAIL.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;8. ALL REQUIRED EXITS SHALL BE OPERABLE FROM THE INSIDE, WITHOUT THE USE OF A KEY OR ANY SPECIAL KNOWLEDGE. \P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c
  3
0|p34;9. ANY ELECTRICAL, PLUMBING AND/OR HVAC SYSTEMS INCLUDED IN THE WORK SHALL BE INSTALLED ON A DESIGN-BUILD BASIS, AND SHALL NOT SIGNIFICANTLY ALTER THE STRUCTURE OR FINISHES.\P\P10. SMOKE DETECTORS AND CARBON MONOXIDE DETECTORS SHALL BE INSTALLE
  3
D PER APPLICABLE CODES.\P\P11. GRADING AND SITEWORK SHALL BE MINIMAL IN ALL AREAS NOT DIRECTLY AFFECTED BY THE NEW CONSTRUCTION. FOLLOW BEST PRACTICES AND LOCAL REQUIREMENTS IN ORDER TO MINIMIZE ENVIRONMENTAL DAMAGE.\P\P12. FINISH GRADE MUST SLOPE AW
  3
AY FROM EXTERIOR FOUNDATION WALL, AT A HEIGHT OF 6 INCHES OVER A 10 FOOT DISTANCE.\P\P13. ANY SURVEY MARKERS WITHIN THE AREA OF CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE PRESERVED OR RESET BY A REGISTERED CIVIL ENGINEER OR LICENSED LAND SURVEYOR.\P\P14. BEFORE GRADING O
  1
PERATIONS, A TEMPORARY PROTECTION FENCE SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED AROUND ANY TREE WITHIN 30 FEET OF THE FOUNDATION, AND A SILT FENCE MUST BE CONSTRUCTED DOWNSLOPE OF ANY AREA WHERE THE SOIL IS DISTURBED.}
