{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;15. DEPICTED FOUNDATION SHOWS ONLY A PROPOSED DESIGN BASED ON FICTIONAL CONDITIONS. CONDUCT A SOIL TEST AND STRUCTURAL ENGINEERING FOR A SITE-SPECIFIC FOUNDATION.\P\P16. FOOTINGS SHALL EXTEND DOWN BEYOND THE LOCAL FROST LINE. \P
  3
\P17. PERFORATED DRAIN PIPES SHALL BE LOCATED WITHIN A GRAVEL PERIMETER AROUND THE FOUNDATION, WITH MULTIPLE DRAINAGE OUTLETS LEADING DOWNSLOPE AWAY FROM THE BUILDING.\P\P\H1.00001x;18. FIRE BLOCKING AND FIRE-RATED SHEATHING SHALL BE PROVIDED AS REQU
  3
IRED AT CEILINGS, FLOORS, AND ENCLOSED USABLE SPACE UNDER STAIRS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H0.99999x;19. ALL WOOD WITHIN 8 INCHES OF THE GROUND SHALL BE PRESSURE TREATED OR COMPRISE A SUITABLY ROT RESISTANT MATERIAL. MET
  3
AL CONNECTIONS WHICH TOUCH THIS WOOD SHOULD BE GALVANIZED OR STAINLESS STEEL.\P\P20 PROVIDE ADEQUATE BLOCKING AROUND CABINETRY, PLUMBING FIXTURES, AND OTHER APPLICABLE AREAS.\P\P21. PROVIDE MINIMUM R-13 INSULATION IN ALL EXTERIOR WALLS AND R-21 INSUL
  3
ATION AT ROOFS OF CONDITIONED SPACES.\P\P22. DEPICTED WEATHERPROOFING METHODS (SUCH AS SEALANT, CAULKING, AND FLASHING) ARE NOT COMPREHENSIVE. FOLLOW REQUIREMENTS AND RECOMMENDATIONS OF BUILDING CODES, PRODUCT MANUFACTURERS, AND CONSTRUCTION BEST PRA
  1
CTICES.}
