{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H0.500006x;34. PROVIDE TEMPORARY SUPPORT AS NECESSARY TO ENSURE THE STRUCTURAL INTEGRITY OF THE BUILDING UNDER CONSTRUCTION. THE GENERAL CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL CONSTRUCTION-RELATED ACTIVITIES.\P\P\H0.999988x;35. INST
  3
ALL FIXTURES, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT ACCORDING TO MANUFACTURER'S SPECIFICATIONS. SHOULD THOSE SPECS CONFLICT WITH THE DRAWINGS, IMMEDIATELY NOTIFY THE OWNER OR THE OWNER'S REPRESENTATIVE.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34;\P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H1.000
  3
01x;36. VERIFY CLEARANCES FOR FIXTURES, VENTS, CHASES, ETC. BEFORE ORDERING OR INSTALLING RELATED WORK ITEMS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34;\P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H0.99999x;37. COORDINATE ALL WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED 
  3
TO: IRRIGATION PIPES, ELECTRICAL CONDUITS, WATER LINES, GAS LINES, AND DRAINAGE LINES.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H1.00001x; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;38. THE GENERAL CONTRACTOR SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR REGULARLY REMOVING THE WASTE MATERIALS OF ALL 
  3
SUBCONTRACTORS, AND MAINTAIN STRICT CONTROL OVER JOB CLEANING TO PREVENT DUST AND RUBBISH FROM INTERFERING WITH OPERATIONS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;39. CONSTRUCTION EQUIPMENT NOISE SHALL BE MINIMIZED DURING THE CONSTRUCT
  1
ION PHASES BY MUFFLING AND SHIELDING IMPACT TOOLS WHENEVER POSSIBLE.}
